# The Conservatory on orchid: /etc/conservatory/conservatory.env
# Root-owned, mode 0600. Read by both units through EnvironmentFile=. Never
# in the repo; Servers/install-orchid.sh copies this example into place when
# the file does not exist yet and asks you to fill in the key.

# The one SQLite file, created and migrated by Fern. Outside the checkout
# (a deploy can never touch it), beside the photos.
CONSERVATORY_DB=/home/todd/conservatory-data/conservatory.db

# The photo tree, photos/yyyy/mm/<uuid>.jpg and their thumbnails, and the
# species reference images Fern fetches from Wikipedia, reference/<id>.jpg.
CONSERVATORY_DATA=/home/todd/conservatory-data

# Pl@ntNet API key (https://my.plantnet.org). Fern only; the web app never
# calls Pl@ntNet. Free tier: 500 identifications a day.
PLANTNET_API_KEY=

# Vercel AI Gateway key (https://vercel.com/ai-gateway), for the care sheets
# Fern writes once per species. Optional: empty, Fern runs without them and
# the species page says so. Fern calls the model; the web app only checks
# that the key is set, to offer Rewrite.
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# The gateway's model slug for care sheets. Unset means this one.
#CONSERVATORY_LLM=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5

# The household's USDA hardiness zone, 1 to 13 with an optional a or b. Care
# sheets say what it means here; changing it has Fern rewrite every sheet.
#CONSERVATORY_ZONE=6a
